# the hero-frame checklist input (TUI-DESIGN-3 §9 V1–V21): chat-task's path — settle, a greeting (an intake reply), a task (a mock run with
# one `[step N]` row per step), the epilogue, the mark back under the strip — then scripts/pty/polish-check.mjs runs over the .cap/.txt pair
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* Hi\.
mark hi-reply
sleep 0.3
send fix the failing test
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*fix the failing test
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* start 
expect \[step 1\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
expect end (complete|max_steps|generator_done)
expect Follow-up, question
sleep 0.5
send /cost
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect raise: /budget
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
